  "hints": [
    "The answer is a contiguous window of length k. Which window?",
    "Binary search the window's left edge `L` in `[0, n-k]`: compare `x - nums[mid]` with `nums[mid+k] - x`.",
    "lo, hi = 0, n - k\nwhile lo < hi:\n    mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n    if x - nums[mid] > nums[mid + k] - x: lo = mid + 1\n    else: hi = mid\nreturn nums[lo : lo + k]",
    "If `nums[mid+k]` is closer than `nums[mid]`, the window should slide right. Binary search over left edges is O(log(n - k) + k)."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(log n + k)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
